       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in SSSS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " start empiric IV antistaphylococcal abx immediately; typically nafcillin or oxacillin until improvement, then oral dicloxacillin; first-generation cephalosporins (eg, cefazolin, cephalexin) are alternatives."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Serious prior allergic rxn to a penicillin. Most pts who report penicillin allergy don't rxt on re-exposure; w a vague or inconsistent Hx and ⍉effective or convenient alt, skin testing may be done."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Probenecid blocks renal tubular secretion and raises penicillin levels."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
